// ═══ DEADLOCK: threads BLOCKED, waiting for each other ═══
// Thread-1: lock(A) → wait for B (held by T2)
// Thread-2: lock(B) → wait for A (held by T1)
// Both BLOCKED! State: BLOCKED. Zero CPU usage.
// Detection: jstack → "Found Java-level deadlock"
//            ThreadMXBean.findDeadlockedThreads() → thread IDs!
// Fix: lock ordering, tryLock, avoid nested locks

// ═══ LIVELOCK: threads RUNNING but no progress ═══
// Thread-1: try lock(A) → try lock(B) → fail → release A → retry
// Thread-2: try lock(B) → try lock(A) → fail → release B → retry
// Both keep retrying! State: RUNNABLE. HIGH CPU. Zero throughput!
// Detection: CPU 100% + zero throughput! Thread dump: RUNNABLE threads
//            doing tryLock/release loops. No "deadlock" in jstack.
// Fix: random backoff! Thread.sleep(random * 2^attempt) before retry

// ═══ STARVATION: thread never gets its turn ═══
// Non-fair ReentrantLock: new threads "barge in" ahead of waiting threads
// Low-priority thread: scheduler always picks higher-priority threads
// Reader starvation: write lock holders always arrive → readers starve
// Detection: one thread's wait time >> others. Monitor wait metrics.
// Fix: fair lock (new ReentrantLock(true)), equal thread priorities

// ═══ COMPARISON ═══
// Hazard      Thread State   CPU   Progress   Detection
// Deadlock    BLOCKED        0%    none       jstack "deadlock", ThreadMXBean
// Livelock    RUNNABLE       100%  none       CPU + zero throughput
// Starvation  WAITING/BLOCKED varies partial  long wait times, fairness metrics

// ═══ LIVELOCK CODE EXAMPLE ═══
ReentrantLock lockA = new ReentrantLock();
ReentrantLock lockB = new ReentrantLock();

// Thread-1:
while (true) {
    lockA.lock();
        if (lockB.tryLock()) { try { doWork();
        break; } finally { lockB.unlock(); lockA.unlock(); } }
    lockA.unlock();  // give up A, retry
    // Thread.sleep(random);  ← FIX: add random backoff!
}
// Thread-2: same but lockB first, then lockA
// Without backoff: both keep acquiring/releasing in sync → livelock!
// With random backoff: one sleeps longer → other gets both → progress!
